{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q407125","formula":"AlH₃O₃","hill":"AlH3O3","elements":["H","O","Al"],"composition":{"H":3.0,"O":3.0,"Al":1.0},"names":{"en":"Aluminum hydroxide","ru":"Гидроксид алюминия","uk":"Гідроксид алюмінію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Aluminium hydroxide, Al(OH)3, is a white chemical compound that is found as the mineral gibbsite (also known as hydrargillite) and its three much rarer polymorphs: bayerite, doyleite, and nordstrandite. Aluminium hydroxide is amphoteric, meaning it has both basic and acidic properties. Closely related are aluminium oxide hydroxide, AlO(OH), and aluminium oxide or alumina (Al2O3), the latter of which is also amphoteric.","ru":"Гидрокси́д алюми́ния — неорганическое соединение с химической формулой Al(OH)3. Белое студенистое вещество, плохо растворимое в воде, обладает амфотерными свойствами, слабый электролит.","uk":"Гідрокси́д алюмі́нію Al(OH)3 — безбарвна порошкоподібна речовина. У воді практично не розчиняється."},"fame":51,"pubchemCid":10176082,"mass":78.004,"charge":0,"smiles":"[OH-].[OH-].[OH-].[Al+3]","inchikey":"WNROFYMDJYEPJX-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"aluminum trihydroxide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-27540","atoms":56,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[8.751,0.0,0.0],[0.0,5.113,0.0],[-8.407,0.0,9.689]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":1.615,"y":2.43,"z":4.823,"el":"Al"},{"x":2.932,"y":4.986,"z":0.022,"el":"Al"},{"x":-1.272,"y":2.683,"z":4.866,"el":"Al"},{"x":-2.588,"y":0.127,"z":9.667,"el":"Al"},{"x":3.08,"y":4.943,"z":4.827,"el":"Al"},{"x":1.467,"y":2.387,"z":0.018,"el":"Al"},{"x":-2.736,"y":0.169,"z":4.862,"el":"Al"},{"x":-1.124,"y":2.726,"z":9.671,"el":"Al"},{"x":6.122,"y":1.737,"z":2.848,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.575,"y":4.293,"z":1.996,"el":"H"},{"x":-5.778,"y":3.376,"z":6.84,"el":"H"},{"x":1.919,"y":0.82,"z":7.6